    <div class="section" id="s11">
      <p class="sec-num">11 —</p>
      <h2>Knowledge Check</h2>
      <p>Test your understanding of networking fundamentals with these five quick questions.</p>

      <div class="quiz-container">
        <!-- Quiz 1 -->
        <div class="quiz-card" id="q1">
          <div class="quiz-q">1. Which OSI layer is responsible for logical addressing and routing data across different
            networks?</div>
          <div class="quiz-options">
            <div class="quiz-opt">Data Link Layer (Layer 2)</div>
            <div class="quiz-opt">Network Layer (Layer 3)</div>
            <div class="quiz-opt">Transport Layer (Layer 4)</div>
            <div class="quiz-opt">Session Layer (Layer 5)</div>
          </div>
          <div class="quiz-feedback" id="f1"></div>
        </div>

        <!-- Quiz 2 -->
        <div class="quiz-card" id="q2">
          <div class="quiz-q">2. What is the main difference between TCP and UDP?</div>
          <div class="quiz-options">
            <div class="quiz-opt">TCP is used for websites, UDP is used for emails.</div>
            <div class="quiz-opt">TCP is faster but less reliable than UDP.</div>
            <div class="quiz-opt">TCP is connection-oriented and reliable; UDP is
              connectionless and "best-effort".</div>
            <div class="quiz-opt">There is no functional difference; they are
              interchangeable.</div>
          </div>
          <div class="quiz-feedback" id="f2"></div>
        </div>

        <!-- Quiz 3 -->
        <div class="quiz-card" id="q3">
          <div class="quiz-q">3. What is the role of the Domain Name System (DNS)?</div>
          <div class="quiz-options">
            <div class="quiz-opt">To encrypt web traffic using TLS.</div>
            <div class="quiz-opt">To assign dynamic IP addresses to devices.</div>
            <div class="quiz-opt">To translate human-readable domain names into IP
              addresses.</div>
            <div class="quiz-opt">To route packets between different ISPs.</div>
          </div>
          <div class="quiz-feedback" id="f3"></div>
        </div>

        <!-- Quiz 4 -->
        <div class="quiz-card" id="q4">
          <div class="quiz-q">4. Which protocol is considered the "glue" that holds the Internet together by routing
            traffic between Autonomous Systems?</div>
          <div class="quiz-options">
            <div class="quiz-opt">HTTP</div>
            <div class="quiz-opt">BGP (Border Gateway Protocol)</div>
            <div class="quiz-opt">DHCP</div>
            <div class="quiz-opt">ICMP</div>
          </div>
          <div class="quiz-feedback" id="f4"></div>
        </div>

        <!-- Quiz 5 -->
        <div class="quiz-card" id="q5">
          <div class="quiz-q">5. What does NAT (Network Address Translation) allow a home router to do?</div>
          <div class="quiz-options">
            <div class="quiz-opt">Increase the speed of the internet connection.</div>
            <div class="quiz-opt">Assign multiple public IP addresses to a single device.
            </div>
            <div class="quiz-opt">Allow multiple devices in a private network to share a
              single public IP address.</div>
            <div class="quiz-opt">Automatically update the router's firmware.</div>
          </div>
          <div class="quiz-feedback" id="f5"></div>
        </div>

        <div class="retake-container" id="retake-container">
          <button class="retake-btn">Retake Quiz</button>
